cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: A Differentially Private Release for Synthetic Tabular Data, Decodable by Any Generator"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.2.5"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22945315"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  Differentially private synthetic tabular data is produced today by marginal mechanisms, which
  choose their workload on the private rows and ship a fitted model, or by language models
  fine-tuned or driven under the budget, inseparable from the mechanism that spends it. We propose
  CoRTeC, which separates the two. CoRTeC spends the privacy budget once, on a small release of
  noisy counts designed for training a classifier. For each cohort of the data, the release gives
  the cohort's size, its class balance, a histogram of every attribute for each outcome class, and
  the outcome rate in a set of non-overlapping cells. A reviewer can check every one of these
  numbers before the release leaves the institution. Everything after the release is
  post-processing and costs no further privacy. A maximum-entropy decoder can turn the counts into
  rows, and so can each of the five frozen language models we tested, none of which ever sees a
  record. A selection step then matches the decoded rows to the released counts. One release can
  therefore serve any number of draws, by any team and with any model, and the model can be
  replaced without touching the guarantee. At ε = 2, the auto-configured release, decoded without
  a language model, trains classifiers to within 0.02 AUC of a real sample of the same size on
  Adult, over three splits. The gap is larger on NHANES and bank marketing, reaching 0.07 AUC on
  the medical dataset. In five of the six dataset-size settings, its utility reaches that of the
  reference AIM, whose adaptive workload fits pairs of columns more closely. The language model's
  contribution comes from the column names, and without the release it copies the public file. No
  private row ever reaches a decoder, the strongest membership attack stays far below the bound
  the budget allows, and no synthetic row copies a training row. This repository holds the
  Apache-2.0 reference implementation with its tests, the research pipeline, the paper, the
  deployment guide and the frozen auto-configurations.
